<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kadriah Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1771">1771</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Istana Kadriah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kadriah Palace is the wooden palace of the sultans of Pontianak in West Kalimantan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, at the meeting of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapuas-river">Kapuas</a> and Landak rivers. It was begun in 1771 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syarif-abdurrahman-alkadrie">Syarif Abdurrahman Alkadrie</a>, founder of the city and sultanate, near his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jami">Jami</a> mosque. It is now a museum holding royal regalia and furniture.</p></div>
